# chatRuleAnyrankPush(Player player)
# One-shot rule-explanation chat: fires the first time the player
# witnesses a pawn double-push from a non-starting rank (variant
# rule — pawns can double-push from ANY rank, not just rank 2/7).
# noticeVariantRules dispatches here and sets the seenAnyrankPushRule
# flag so this never fires twice for the same player. Standard
# starting-rank double pushes do NOT trigger this — they're normal
# chess.
#
# Body is a TEST PLACEHOLDER — replace with the real explanation
# wording / random pick from a flavor pool. Keep the (player)
# signature so the trigger stays unchanged.

@using rychess
@fast

@delay 65
@player &aRYgamer1&7 -> You: oh btw pawns can move 2 spaces from any rank here, not just the starting one lol
